        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="0791" n="477" xml:id="pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 840.48/126</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Austria-Hungary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Penfield</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-09">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 10, 7:30 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Austro-Hungarian Government agrees to exemption from military law such vessels as
                    may be chartered by Americans for transportation citizens to the United States
                    on condition that vessels are used exclusively for purpose named and that other
                    belligerent states agree to proposal. They ask to be kept fully informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Penfield</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
